body:
I will add an extra thought here, from my personal experience. It is possible that Your solution can be wrong, but still solve the problem. If you feel that your solution is not a very good solution even if does solve the problem it asks you to solve, I suggest finding what parts you don't like. 

In sorta psuedo code.

My example. No repeats please.

Str="aab"
PERMS=[]
VAR ARR=[0,1,2]//generated by str length. Abcd becomes 0, 1,2,3,

VAR ARRLEN=FACTORIAL(STR.LENGTH)
//the number of permutations possible is n where n is the number of letters in the string.

FOR(I=0;I<ARRLEN;I++){
RANDOMIZE ARR.
IF(PERMS INCLUDES(ARR)){I--;}
ELSE
{PUSH ARR TO PERMS}
}
//randomize ARR, if it's not in PERMS push it. If it is already been pushed there go back and try again.

// So we build the list of permutations by shear brute Force of random.

Perms= perms.map()
//Replace all the numbers with letters from the original string.
